  "title": "An injection phrase is content, never proof, and never moves the verdict",
  "description": "Otherwise identical to Scenario A (a fully-verified legitimate request) except the caller opens with an instruction-injection phrase lifted straight from the injection lexicon (\"ignore previous instructions\"). The injection_marker card FLAGs (provenance CALLER_SAID, quoted verbatim) and the rulebook counts it 0 toward the tally by design -- decide() never even reads injection_marker. Proves the verdict is computed purely from the evidence that actually matters: this call still reaches STAGE, exactly as if the phrase had never been said, because content in a transcript can never talk its way to a different verdict.",
